{
 "encounter_id": "00744",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Morning. It's my eyelid, it's been twitching for weeks. Left one. Drives me mad."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "How many weeks?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Three, I think. Or four. Since the Easter break."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Is it there all day, or at certain times?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "When I'm tired, mostly. And at my desk. It comes and goes, ten seconds, a minute."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Does your eye close fully, or does the eyelid droop?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, no drooping. It just flickers."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any double vision, or twitching elsewhere on your face?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No double vision. And no, only the eyelid."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Okay. Let's see what you're taking."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Sertraline, 50 mg once a day. And propranolol, 40 mg, maybe? For the shakes, when I need it. I'd have to check the box."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'll check that on the record, thank you. Any other medical history?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Anxiety, which is why the tablets. Migraines. And hay fever."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "How much caffeine are you having? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Five or six coffees, I'm afraid. And energy drinks. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And how's your sleep? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Poor. Five hours a night, since the new project. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me check your pulse and blood pressure. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Go on. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Pulse 78, blood pressure 124 over 80.",
   "pause": 12.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Is that okay? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Fine. You'll be glad to hear this is a very common benign twitch, caused by tiredness, stress and caffeine, and it settles when those do. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "It's not a nerve thing? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Nothing you've described suggests a nerve problem. No droop, no double vision, no other muscles. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Right. That's a relief. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Cut your caffeine down to two cups, none after lunch, and no energy drinks."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "That's going to hurt. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Try for seven hours' sleep, and take screen breaks every hour, with a few minutes of eyes closed."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I'll set an alarm. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Most twitches go in a few weeks once you do that. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "And if it doesn't? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd like to see you again in four weeks. If it's spreading to other parts of the face, or the eyelid starts to droop, come sooner."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I'll write it down. Where's my phone? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "In your hand. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "So it is. Thank you. ~"
  }
 ],
